      "documentConcept": "PD autonomic dysfunction: orthostatic hypotension, constipation, bladder",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:7d2c7d7f69b701c4bea8d8bcfeb6832567fb75d00771bca9028382ce87bf3e6b",
      "text": "This section covers Parkinson\u2019s autonomic symptoms: orthostatic hypotension, constipation and bladder symptoms. OH management combines medication review and nonpharmacological measures with selected drugs while monitoring supine hypertension. Constipation can involve slow transit and impaired evacuation; macrogol and lubiprostone have trial support. The cited review describes bladder assessment as checking coexisting urological disease and medication trade-offs. Antimuscarinics may worsen constipation, while mirabegron trials have differing outcomes. Probiotic recommendations also differ across evidence reviews; product-specific and short-term results should retain their qualifications.",
